# Generated per machine by install-opencode.sh (opencode's counterpart to
# .mcp.json). Anchored to the repo root on purpose: a bare `opencode.json`
# also matched .opencode/opencode.json, which is committed config.
/opencode.json
.gemini/settings.json
data/

# Build-time scratch and template provenance — never committed into an app.
#
# .gova-build/ is the gova-build-execution skill's working directory: task
# briefs, per-task reports, review diffs. It is a record of HOW a build was
# carried out, useful while it runs and noise afterwards. It was not ignored
# before, which is how a 20KB report about fixing the template ended up
# committed and shipping into every project scaffolded from this repo.
.gova-build/

# Notes about developing THIS repo (the template) rather than an app built with
# it. A derived project inherits every tracked file, and an AI opening that
# project reads them as its own project's history — spending context on, and
# sometimes reasoning from, decisions that belong to somebody else's codebase.
docs/gova-monolith-history/

